  "observations": [
    "The native floor is inclusive at twice square-root epsilon. Native captures cover a shallow polygon, a rational quarter circle and a nonuniform cubic line below, at and just above the threshold. Both preparation entry points now retain the same disabled-fit policy.",
    "Physical G2 curvature tolerance determines the C0/C1 region boundary. The existing general continuity query keeps its default policy; the new native adapter permits explicit curvature tolerances in inverse model units.",
    "C1 reconstruction retimes the raw curve before Hermite evaluation. Global Greville interpolation after retiming did not reproduce the native controls and was rejected.",
    "Thirty-one complete native surface definitions match the new proposal followed by existing common-basis preparation at 1e-9 on both backends. This establishes the measured joining construction, not general adaptive subdivision decisions.",
    "A three-station adaptive acceptance model was refuted by unequal, reversed and tiny-tolerance holdouts. Seven-station raw proposals remain separate from command acceptance. Their source certificates remain authoritative regardless of native control-net differences.",
    "Isolated intervals accept one cubic across translations, reversals and source clocks. Public cubic-Bezier construction produces different pieces from paired native Loft preparation. These observations remain frozen as counterexamples, without admitting their unresolved command fits.",
    "Curved-source adaptive experiments differed from native controls or bases and were withdrawn. Existing qualified initial and corrected smooth proposals remain unchanged."
  ],
